WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.100 --> 00:00:04.933
Aj Caldwell: Yeah!

00:00:04.933 --> 00:00:07.330
Caroline Aghajanian: On this
episode of "Travel Dares,"

00:00:07.330 --> 00:00:09.390
Aj: I'm taking Caroline to Area 47,

00:00:09.390 --> 00:00:12.340
where we're going down a
massive, 55-foot waterslide.

00:00:12.340 --> 00:00:13.665
Caroline: And I'm taking Aj to

00:00:13.665 --> 00:00:15.820
a former Olympic bobsled course,

00:00:15.820 --> 00:00:18.170
where we'll see how fast we go.

00:00:18.170 --> 00:00:19.820
Come join us on our adventures

00:00:19.820 --> 00:00:22.183
on this episode of "Travel Dares."

00:00:24.950 --> 00:00:26.530
This is "Travel Dares,"

00:00:26.530 --> 00:00:29.620
the show where we do daring
activities all across Europe,

00:00:29.620 --> 00:00:32.470
empowered by my Marriott
Bonvoy Boundless card.

00:00:32.470 --> 00:00:33.860
Aj, where are we?

00:00:33.860 --> 00:00:36.030
Aj: We are in Innsbruck, Austria.

00:00:36.030 --> 00:00:38.420
Innsbruck is located in
the heart of the Alps,

00:00:38.420 --> 00:00:41.220
and it's perfect for anyone
looking for an adventure.

00:00:41.220 --> 00:00:43.690
And speaking of an adventure,

00:00:43.690 --> 00:00:45.020
are you ready for your first clue?

00:00:45.020 --> 00:00:46.790
Caroline: I am so ready, I'm so excited.

00:00:46.790 --> 00:00:47.623
OK.

00:00:50.350 --> 00:00:51.210
OK.

00:00:51.210 --> 00:00:53.580
Flying over Austria.

00:00:53.580 --> 00:00:55.470
How high are we flying, though?

00:00:55.470 --> 00:00:58.837
Aj: Just enough to make
you nervous. [laughs]

00:00:58.837 --> 00:01:00.432
Caroline: I am, like, 100% sure

00:01:00.432 --> 00:01:02.290
that we're gonna be
jumping off of something.

00:01:02.290 --> 00:01:04.750
I think we might be bungee jumping

00:01:04.750 --> 00:01:08.170
or we might be skydiving.

00:01:08.170 --> 00:01:09.122
Aj: This slide is known for

00:01:09.122 --> 00:01:11.000
shooting people super high in the air,

00:01:11.000 --> 00:01:14.460
and I'm excited to see if
Caroline can stick the landing.

00:01:14.460 --> 00:01:17.540
Caroline: Oh gosh, why
are these steps so steep?

00:01:17.540 --> 00:01:19.360
My heart is beating now.

00:01:19.360 --> 00:01:21.065
Aj: Now, stay right here.

00:01:21.065 --> 00:01:23.625
OK?
Caroline: Where are you going?

00:01:23.625 --> 00:01:24.843
Aj!

00:01:24.843 --> 00:01:25.854
Aj!

00:01:25.854 --> 00:01:26.784
Aj: Yeah?

00:01:26.784 --> 00:01:28.247
Caroline: How much longer?

00:01:28.247 --> 00:01:29.992
Aj: It'll be a while.

00:01:29.992 --> 00:01:32.483
Caroline, take off your blindfold!

00:01:32.483 --> 00:01:34.191
[Caroline laughing]

00:01:34.191 --> 00:01:37.032
Aj: Woo!

00:01:37.032 --> 00:01:39.150
Caroline: Oh, my God!

00:01:39.150 --> 00:01:42.673
Oh, my god! [laughs]

00:01:44.506 --> 00:01:48.317
That's gonna be so much fun!

00:01:56.920 --> 00:01:59.220
OK, I'm so excited,
what do I need to know?

00:01:59.220 --> 00:02:01.010
Michael Auer: So, you just
lie down on your back,

00:02:01.010 --> 00:02:03.410
cross arms and legs, keep body tension,

00:02:03.410 --> 00:02:04.360
and when you're in the air,

00:02:04.360 --> 00:02:06.090
you go forward with your upper body

00:02:06.090 --> 00:02:07.170
so you can land on your feet.

00:02:07.170 --> 00:02:11.460
Caroline: I am so ready to
just, like, fly in the air!

00:02:11.460 --> 00:02:14.740
I am so excited, can we
get up there already?

00:02:14.740 --> 00:02:15.890
Aj: Let's get to the top.

00:02:20.343 --> 00:02:21.560
Both: We're at the top.

00:02:21.560 --> 00:02:22.410
Caroline: We're at the top.

00:02:22.410 --> 00:02:24.066
Aj: Woo!
Caroline: We're at the top.

00:02:24.066 --> 00:02:27.780
Whoa, that's pretty steep.

00:02:27.780 --> 00:02:29.330
Aj: It's a little
nerve-racking from up here.

00:02:29.330 --> 00:02:30.450
Caroline: Yeah.

00:02:30.450 --> 00:02:33.010
So, you pick up speed down
here, and it curves you,

00:02:33.010 --> 00:02:34.177
and pew, pushes you up?

00:02:34.177 --> 00:02:36.920
Aj: Throws you in the air, absolutely.

00:02:36.920 --> 00:02:37.753
Caroline: That's gonna be fun.

00:02:37.753 --> 00:02:39.216
OK, I just go?

00:02:39.216 --> 00:02:40.806
Did you start off sitting?

00:02:40.806 --> 00:02:41.639
Aj: Yeah, you have to.

00:02:41.639 --> 00:02:42.472
Caroline: OK.

00:02:43.972 --> 00:02:45.180
OK, I'm just gonna do it.

00:02:45.180 --> 00:02:46.550
I'm just gonna go, OK.

00:02:46.550 --> 00:02:48.970
All right, bye! [screams]

00:02:53.189 --> 00:02:54.108
[water splashing]

00:02:55.800 --> 00:02:59.378
Woo! [laughs]

00:02:59.378 --> 00:03:01.940
Oh, my god, I forgot how to swim.

00:03:01.940 --> 00:03:05.560
Oh, my gosh, my body is still shaking,

00:03:05.560 --> 00:03:07.963
and my heart is beating, like,
a thousand beats a minute.

00:03:07.963 --> 00:03:11.290
Like, this is, it's so scary, you guys!

00:03:11.290 --> 00:03:12.960
It's actually really scary.

00:03:12.960 --> 00:03:15.290
Aj: Caroline, how did it
feel flying through the air?

00:03:15.290 --> 00:03:16.820
Caroline: It was so much fun,

00:03:16.820 --> 00:03:19.260
it was, like, so exhilarating,
I'm ready to do it again.

00:03:19.260 --> 00:03:20.593
Aj: Let's do it.
Caroline: Let's go.

00:03:35.319 --> 00:03:37.588
[Caroline screaming]

00:03:37.588 --> 00:03:39.940
We went down, good job.

00:03:39.940 --> 00:03:41.330
I would say good job to me too, though.

00:03:41.330 --> 00:03:42.990
Aj: Good job, good job to you,

00:03:42.990 --> 00:03:44.200
you slayed the dare.

00:03:44.200 --> 00:03:45.920
Caroline: I'm getting a five out of five.

00:03:45.920 --> 00:03:47.520
I can feel it, I can sense it.

00:03:47.520 --> 00:03:49.020
Aj, that was such a thrill,

00:03:49.020 --> 00:03:52.080
but I have a feeling yours
is a little bit more.

00:03:52.080 --> 00:03:53.113
Aj: Give me that clue.

00:03:55.633 --> 00:03:56.820
I can hold on tight.

00:03:56.820 --> 00:04:00.410
Caroline: OK, I hope so,
because you're gonna have to.

00:04:00.410 --> 00:04:02.700
Aj: I don't even have a guess for this.

00:04:02.700 --> 00:04:04.640
I don't know what to think about it,

00:04:04.640 --> 00:04:07.160
but my stomach is tingling
just a little bit.

00:04:07.160 --> 00:04:09.110
Innsbruck is known as a destination

00:04:09.110 --> 00:04:10.760
for all winter sports,

00:04:10.760 --> 00:04:12.360
and it's one of the only places

00:04:12.360 --> 00:04:14.290
where you can bobsled in the summer.

00:04:14.290 --> 00:04:15.590
OK, we're gonna stop here,

00:04:15.590 --> 00:04:17.940
you're gonna take a really big step

00:04:17.940 --> 00:04:21.380
with your left leg, a
little more, a little more.

00:04:21.380 --> 00:04:23.225
Aj: Wait, wait, oh, like this.

00:04:23.225 --> 00:04:25.530
Caroline: Yes [laughs]. OK, now sit down.

00:04:25.530 --> 00:04:28.120
I'm gonna have you hold on to something.

00:04:28.120 --> 00:04:29.703
Aj: OK, so this is the "hold on tight"?

00:04:29.703 --> 00:04:32.514
Caroline: Yes, now take
off your blindfold,

00:04:32.514 --> 00:04:34.266
because we're going bobsledding!

00:04:34.266 --> 00:04:35.266
Aj: Oh, what?!

00:04:36.550 --> 00:04:38.114
Oh, I've always wanted to do that.

00:04:38.114 --> 00:04:38.947
Caroline: Really?

00:04:38.947 --> 00:04:40.090
[both laughing]

00:04:40.090 --> 00:04:41.006
Caroline: Yes, look at this!
Aj: It's gonna be like

00:04:41.006 --> 00:04:41.839
"Cool Runnings"!

00:04:41.839 --> 00:04:44.650
Caroline: It's gonna be
so fun, so hold on tight.

00:04:44.650 --> 00:04:45.817
Aj: All right.

00:04:54.390 --> 00:04:57.300
Birgit Knauseder: This is
the official bobsled track

00:04:57.300 --> 00:05:00.960
for the Olympics, built in 1964.

00:05:00.960 --> 00:05:03.440
It's the only track in Austria

00:05:03.440 --> 00:05:05.310
where guests can go down in a bobsled

00:05:05.310 --> 00:05:06.500
with a professional driver,

00:05:06.500 --> 00:05:09.330
and it's about 100 kilometers per hour.

00:05:09.330 --> 00:05:10.482
Caroline: I am super stoked.

00:05:10.482 --> 00:05:12.000
They said it's gonna take about a minute

00:05:12.000 --> 00:05:13.920
and five, six seconds to go down.

00:05:13.920 --> 00:05:15.250
I think we can beat that.

00:05:15.250 --> 00:05:16.790
Aj: I think we should
shoot for under a minute.

00:05:16.790 --> 00:05:18.454
Caroline: OK, under a minute, got it.

00:05:18.454 --> 00:05:19.287
Aj: That's the goal.

00:05:19.287 --> 00:05:20.228
Caroline: Safety is first, guys, so.

00:05:20.228 --> 00:05:21.061
Aj: Safety first.

00:05:21.061 --> 00:05:22.430
Caroline: Gotta put on
our...whatcha call them?

00:05:22.430 --> 00:05:23.263
Aj: Sock hat.

00:05:23.263 --> 00:05:24.313
Caroline: A sock hat.
Aj: They're sock hats.

00:05:24.313 --> 00:05:25.400
Caroline: OK, here we go.

00:05:25.400 --> 00:05:27.970
Aj: That is the professional,
technical, official term.

00:05:27.970 --> 00:05:29.680
Caroline [groaning]: Is this correct?

00:05:29.680 --> 00:05:31.706
I feel so professional.

00:05:31.706 --> 00:05:32.539
Aj: Oh, yeah.

00:05:32.539 --> 00:05:33.528
Caroline: Oh, I got a big head.

00:05:33.528 --> 00:05:35.080
[both laughing]

00:05:36.880 --> 00:05:38.980
Aj: I am so ready for this.

00:05:38.980 --> 00:05:40.870
I'm going to crush this dare,

00:05:40.870 --> 00:05:42.540
I'm gonna get my five stars,

00:05:42.540 --> 00:05:44.874
and I'm gonna have a great time doing it.

00:05:50.528 --> 00:05:51.660
Here we go!

00:05:51.660 --> 00:05:53.363
Caroline: Here we go.

00:05:53.363 --> 00:05:55.771
Aj: Nice, slow start.
Nice and easy, Caroline.

00:05:55.771 --> 00:05:57.812
We can handle this part.

00:05:57.812 --> 00:05:59.600
Caroline: OK. OK, we're picking up.

00:05:59.600 --> 00:06:01.241
Aj: Coming up on curve No. 1.

00:06:01.241 --> 00:06:02.824
Caroline: We're picking up.

00:06:03.949 --> 00:06:05.283
Aj: Here we go.
Caroline: Oh, my god!

00:06:06.191 --> 00:06:07.653
Oh my god!
Aj: I can handle that!

00:06:07.653 --> 00:06:09.626
Oh, it's a big one!

00:06:09.626 --> 00:06:12.804
Caroline: Oh God, it's
picking up really fast!

00:06:12.804 --> 00:06:16.226
[both screaming]

00:06:16.226 --> 00:06:17.376
Aj: Whoa!
Caroline: Oh, my God!

00:06:17.376 --> 00:06:19.125
Oh, my God!

00:06:19.125 --> 00:06:21.875
[both screaming]

00:06:25.314 --> 00:06:28.709
OK, one minute feels like 500 minutes!

00:06:28.709 --> 00:06:29.542
Oh, oh!

00:06:30.826 --> 00:06:32.450
We made it!

00:06:32.450 --> 00:06:36.721
That was so much scarier than
I thought it was gonna be!

00:06:36.721 --> 00:06:40.773
I am sweating out of
every pore in my body!

00:06:41.790 --> 00:06:43.151
Lisa, did we make our time?

00:06:43.151 --> 00:06:44.081
Aj: What was the time?

00:06:44.081 --> 00:06:45.516
Lisa: One minute, 20 seconds.

00:06:45.516 --> 00:06:46.349
Caroline: Aw.

00:06:46.349 --> 00:06:47.182
Lisa: You were pretty average.

00:06:47.182 --> 00:06:49.070
Caroline: We're pretty average, it's OK.

00:06:49.070 --> 00:06:50.428
The speed was fast.

00:06:50.428 --> 00:06:51.761
Aj: That was such an adrenaline rush.

00:06:51.761 --> 00:06:52.870
It was awesome!

00:06:56.470 --> 00:06:58.660
Caroline: Innsbruck is one
of the most beautiful places

00:06:58.660 --> 00:06:59.790
I've ever visited.

00:06:59.790 --> 00:07:01.960
Aj: Yeah, and it's really
packed with adventure.

00:07:01.960 --> 00:07:04.410
Caroline: It has such an
amazing view of the Alps.

00:07:04.410 --> 00:07:08.160
Aj, I slipped and I slid
down the ramp to the water,

00:07:08.160 --> 00:07:09.320
how did I do?

00:07:09.320 --> 00:07:12.550
Aj: Caroline, you were
so excited for the dare,

00:07:12.550 --> 00:07:15.150
you went down the slide a million times.

00:07:15.150 --> 00:07:18.980
You did flips, cannonballs, spins,

00:07:18.980 --> 00:07:21.450
and you really made a
splash with that dare.

00:07:21.450 --> 00:07:23.530
So, for that, I can't give you anything

00:07:23.530 --> 00:07:25.354
other than a five-star rating.

00:07:25.354 --> 00:07:26.779
Caroline: Whee, yes!

00:07:28.240 --> 00:07:31.500
I love a good five
stars. I was born to fly.

00:07:31.500 --> 00:07:33.340
Aj, you took bobsledding like a champ.

00:07:33.340 --> 00:07:35.030
I always knew you were
a competitive person,

00:07:35.030 --> 00:07:38.250
and you really, really wanted
to beat that average time,

00:07:38.250 --> 00:07:40.650
and we didn't quite get there,

00:07:40.650 --> 00:07:43.530
and for that you're gonna
have to get a silver,

00:07:43.530 --> 00:07:45.363
you're getting a four out of five.

00:07:46.480 --> 00:07:47.700
Aj: I can take a four.

00:07:47.700 --> 00:07:48.800
I can take a four.
Caroline: It's still good,

00:07:48.800 --> 00:07:50.120
you still get a medal.

00:07:50.120 --> 00:07:53.500
Aj, I'm having such an amazing
time traveling with you.

00:07:53.500 --> 00:07:54.790
Aj: I'm having a great time, too.

00:07:54.790 --> 00:07:56.560
Thanks for showing me around Europe.

00:07:56.560 --> 00:07:58.380
Caroline: Thanks for
finding such awesome dares.

00:07:58.380 --> 00:07:59.669
Aj: Cheers.

